  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 247 AM EDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\n- Showers and Storms Tuesday, Heavy Rain and Isolated Severe Possible\n\nConditons should be dry today with high pressure in place across the \narea, before a low deepening in the RRQ of an upper-levle jet will \ndrive a warm front across the area early Tuesday with a cold front \nlater Tuesday bringing shower and thunderstorm potential. Low-level \ndestabilization in conjunction with increased shear from a westerly \njet will support a low chance for gusty winds south of I96. \nDepending on where the boundary stalls, PWATs over 2.0\" will be \nsupportive of a heavy rain threat as well, subject to that \nplacement. \n\n- Low Predictability Heavy Rain Possible Into The Weekend\n\nPredictability falls into mid to late week as the front stalls just \nsouth of the area, with an upper-level pattern dominated by zonal \nflow with embedded shortwaves. These patterns are notoriously hard \nto pin down. Cluster analysis suggests while there may be dry \nperiods, there's not great confidence as to when they will be. A \nstalled boundary with persistent high PWATs favors the heavy rain \nthreat continuing with a WPC Marginal to Slight ERO in place. \n\nAnother mid-level wave, low-level jet, and surface low fall into \nplace going into this weekend. This will bring additional \nshower/thunderstorm potential.",
